Track 1: Jack-Step the Sidewalk Slate
- Story & Context: In the wet summer of 2017, Marcus Thorne found the water-damaged 1991 cassette in a Solihull scrap yard, noticing how the drag of the ruined tape deck accidentally bent a chaotic warehouse acid track into a perfectly harmonious, hypnotic trance. He brought the tape to Eleanor’s chapel studio, where they spent forty-eight hours straight locking a Flemish harpsichord’s plucks to the warped sub-bass pulse coming off the spools. The track captures that breakthrough evening, built around a childhood sidewalk game where stepping on a crack meant shifting your mental state into total stillness. "Step wide on the wet slate or the whole room turns to dust," whispers a muffled tape-degraded voice over the opening harpsichord arpeggio.
