- Story & Context: Written during a week-long residency inside a flooded medieval church, this track focuses on local organist Arthur Pendelton, who lost his hearing in 1990 only to regain a sensation of low-frequency vibrations through his feet during the chapel’s first lie-down rave. Vance mapped Arthur's hand-written pitch diagrams into a 432Hz microtonal scale, allowing the harpsichord to mirror the exact resonant frequency of the church’s damp oak pews. The track builds slowly as a single TB-303 note slides upward across three minutes, mimicking the sensation of rising floodwaters touching cold stone. "Listen through the soles of your shoes until the floor begins to breathe," chant the soft, multi-tracked vocal harmonies in the middle movement.
